ashwin: Heads-up: I'm proposing TF changes to introduce a mixed preemptible spot pool with graceful fallback and eviction backoff. Posting snippet and rollout plan.

ashwin: ```hcl
resource "aws_autoscaling_group" "preemptible_pool" {
  mixed_instances_policy {
    launch_template {
      launch_template_specification {
        launch_template_id = aws_launch_template.gpu_lt.id
        version = "$Latest"
      }
    }
    instances_distribution {
      on_demand_base_capacity = 0
      on_demand_percentage_above_base_capacity = 10
      spot_allocation_strategy = "capacity-optimized"
    }
    override { instance_type = "p4d.24xlarge"; weighted_capacity = 100 }
    override { instance_type = "g5.12xlarge"; weighted_capacity = 12 }
  }
  tag { key = "Team" value = "infra" propagate_at_launch = true }
  tag { key = "Pool" value = "preemptible-gpu" propagate_at_launch = true }
  lifecycle { create_before_destroy = true }
}
```

margo: Thanks — can we ensure health checks and instance draining hooks before SIGTERM? Last time we had sudden evicts and kubelets didn't cordon.

ashwin: Yep — adding ASG lifecycle hooks that call our preemptible-handler SSM document which invokes a NodeDrain lambda. Also setting kubelet "terminationGracePeriodSeconds" to 120 and enabling graceful node shutdown.

lina: Tagging note: need unified tags for billing + pool-id so autoscaler/monitoring can pick them up. Also lock AMI to gpu-ubuntu-2026-03-01 for this rollout.

ashwin: Patch will add tags: {Team=infra,Pool=preemptible-gpu,CostCenter=ml,PoolID=pp-2026-03}. AMI will be a var: `ami_gpu_image = \"ami-0c12ab34gpu\"`.

ben: Concern: pricing swings — if spot price rises we could get mass evictions. Suggest a controller that monitors spot interruption rate and does gradual shift to a small dedicated pool instead of immediate fallback. Keep allocation_strategy = "capacity-optimized" but add price_tolerance logic.

ashwin: Agreed. Proposed additions: a `price_tolerance_pct` TF var (default 25) plus a simple controller (small lambda) that watches ASG metrics. If `interruption_rate > threshold` AND `spot_price_increase_pct > price_tolerance_pct` then move X% traffic to `dedicated-gpu-pool` via our instance_routing tag. We'll also set `capacity_rebalance = false` to avoid aggressive rebalances.

margo: Rollout plan? I'd like a canary in us-west-2 with 1 AZ, 2 preemptible nodes and 1 fallback dedicated. Run 24h smoke on scheduling, p95 inference latency, and node churn.

ashwin: Rollout steps: 1) create TF feature branch with module change -> 2) apply in us-west-2-dev -> 3) smoke tests (scheduling + node drain) -> 4) staging for 48h (monitor metrics) -> 5) prod gradual ramp (10% -> 50% -> 100%) over 72h with automated rollback on thresholds.

lina: Please include a tf plan snippet in the PR and an explicit AMI rotation window (we'll rotate AMI monthly with canary first). Also add a tag `last_ami_rotate=2026-03-15` to ASG.

ashwin: Adding plan output to PR. Example plan lines: 
```
Plan: 3 to add, 2 to change, 1 to destroy.
  + aws_autoscaling_group.preemptible_pool
  ~ aws_launch_template.gpu_lt (new version)
```

